  "candidate_0022": {
    "reason": "The assertion conflates the definition of overfitting with its consequences. While memorizing noise is a hallmark, it is not strictly necessary; a model can overfit by learning spurious correlations that generalize poorly without full memorization (e.g., relying on dataset artifacts like font style in image classification). The 'literal_assertion' claims characterization via memorization, but the ","counterexample"
  : "A model trained on MNIST with heavy regularization may still overfit to specific background textures or slight pixel shifts (noise) without fully memorizing every training instance, demonstrating that overfitting can occur via poor generalization of patterns rather than strict memorization.",
    "sound_as_stated": false
  }
}
